cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "fairmoo_benchmarks"
message: >
  If you use this software, please cite (1) the original MPMOP/MPDMP benchmark
  papers and (2) this Python port repository. Do not attribute authorship of the
  original benchmarks to the port maintainers.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Ferreira da Silva"
    given-names: "Pedro Natanael"
    alias: "pedronatanaelfs"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pedronatanaelfs/benchmarks_python"
url: "https://github.com/pedronatanaelfs/benchmarks_python"
version: "0.1.0"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  Source-traced Python/NumPy/pymoo implementations of multi-party multi-objective
  optimization benchmarks MPMOP1–MPMOP17 and MPDMP1–MPDMP18, with explicit
  decision-maker objective ownership and benchmark-by-benchmark validation status.
keywords:
  - multi-objective optimization
  - multi-party optimization
  - evolutionary computation
  - benchmarks
  - pymoo
